Input: {"question": "When was Sunshine Records established?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80:d00", "start": 0, "end": 116, "text": "Sunshine Records (Australia) Sunshine Records was an Australian independent pop music record label of the mid-1960s."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80:d00", "start": 117, "end": 347, "text": "It was established in late 1964 by promoter Ivan Dayman in collaboration with musician-producer-arranger-songwriter Pat Aulton and entrepreneur, producer and songwriter Nat Kipner (who subsequently founded the Spin Records label)."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80:d00", "start": 348, "end": 623, "text": "Although his enterprise was short-lived, Dayman was arguably the first Australian popular music entrepreneur to create a fully integrated pop music company that included artist management and bookings, record production, record labels, venue management and concert promotion."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80:d00", "start": 624, "end": 685, "text": "Most of the label's releases were made in the period 1965-67."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80:d00", "start": 686, "end": 717, "text": "Its biggest act was solo singer"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80:d01", "start": 0, "end": 116, "text": "Sunshine Records (Australia) Sunshine Records was an Australian independent pop music record label of the mid-1960s."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80:d01", "start": 117, "end": 348, "text": "It was established in early 1970 by promoter Ivan Dayman in collaboration with musician-producer-arranger-songwriter Pat Aulton and entrepreneur, producer and songwriter Nat Kipner (who subsequently founded the Spin Records label)."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80:d01", "start": 349, "end": 624, "text": "Although his enterprise was short-lived, Dayman was arguably the first Australian popular music entrepreneur to create a fully integrated pop music company that included artist management and bookings, record production, record labels, venue management and concert promotion."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80:d01", "start": 625, "end": 686, "text": "Most of the label's releases were made in the period 1970-72."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80:d01", "start": 687, "end": 719, "text": "Its biggest act was solo singer."}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80:d02", "start": 0, "end": 180, "text": "Sunshine Records (United States) Sunshine Records was a small California-based record label of the early 1920s, producing 6 double-sided gramophone records of early jazz and blues."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80:d02", "start": 181, "end": 238, "text": "The labels of Sunshine Records say that they were \"Manuf."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80:d02", "start": 239, "end": 254, "text": "by Spikes Bros."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80:d02", "start": 255, "end": 269, "text": "Phonograph Co."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80:d02", "start": 270, "end": 274, "text": "Inc."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80:d02", "start": 275, "end": 378, "text": "Los Angeles\", but they were all actually manufactured by Nordskog Records, and also issued by Nordskog."}, "D3S7": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80:d02", "start": 379, "end": 463, "text": "Most Sunshine Records simply have the Sunshine label pasted over the Nordskog label."}, "D3S8": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0263-d67a175b3d80:d02", "start": 464, "end": 639, "text":